# Cloudflare Pages — keep the repository's non-public folders off the web.
# Added 2026-10-26 after checking what the site actually serves: the app is
# built from the repository root, so every tracked file ships with it. The
# database schema, the Worker source, the tests and the unbundled sources were
# all readable at their path. None of them carry a secret — that was verified
# separately — but the Worker source states its rate limits and its origin
# allowlist, and a reader of the schema learns the shape of every table. There
# is no reason for any of it to answer a request.
#
# private/ is already safe: it is in .gitignore, so it never reaches the repo
# or the deploy. Dotfiles such as .git are not served by Pages at all.
#
# NOTE 2026-10-26: these rules alone do NOT work. Pages serves an existing
# static asset BEFORE consulting _redirects, so the real blocking is done by
# functions/_middleware.js plus _routes.json. These stay as a second line for
# paths that do not exist at all.
#
# The app itself is logbook.html plus assets/ — nothing below is part of it.
/supabase/*  /404.html  404
/worker/*    /404.html  404
/test/*      /404.html  404
/src/*       /404.html  404
/docs/*      /404.html  404
/node_modules/*  /404.html  404
/package.json     /404.html  404
/package-lock.json  /404.html  404
/build.js    /404.html  404
